Description: Fix CVE-2026-107161 - heap overflow in DIGEST-MD5 add_to_challenge()
 add_to_challenge() sized its output buffer from the unquoted value length.
 When quote() escapes backslash or double-quote characters the value grows,
 but the second _plug_buf_alloc() call was passed the stale (too small)
 newlen, so the following strcat() wrote past the end of the heap buffer.
 A malicious DIGEST-MD5/HTTP Digest server could trigger this in a client via
 a crafted realm or nonce. Recompute newlen from the quoted length before
 reallocating; this also keeps *curlen accurate for later appends.

Origin: ai-synthesized, CVE-2026-107161
Author: Root.io Novel Patcher <security@root.io>
Bug: https://github.com/cyrusimap/cyrus-sasl/issues/889
Last-Update: 2026-10-10

--- a/plugins/digestmd5.c
+++ b/plugins/digestmd5.c
@@ -565,8 +565,10 @@
 	    if (quoted == NULL)
 		MEMERROR(utils);
 	    valuesize = strlen(quoted);
-	    /* As the quoted string is bigger, make sure we have enough
-	       space now */
+	    /* As the quoted string is bigger, recompute the required length
+	       from the quoted size (newlen was computed from the unquoted
+	       value) and make sure we have enough space now */
+	    newlen = (unsigned) (*curlen + 1 + namesize + 2 + valuesize + 2);
 	    ret = _plug_buf_alloc(utils, str, buflen, newlen);
 	    if (ret == SASL_OK) {
 		strcat(*str, quoted);
